# Line endings. Windows users are first class here, and the failure this file
# prevents is SILENT.
#
# Why (first real Windows install of our other tooling, 2026-07-27): a tracked
# text file checked out with CRLF, so a POSIX shell read a value as "name\r",
# matched nothing, and installed nothing without a single error message. Any
# file a script READS AS DATA has the same failure mode, and it is invisible.
#
# Rule: everything is LF in the repo and in the working tree, with two
# deliberate exceptions below.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF or bash reports a bogus syntax error on Windows
# checkouts under WSL / Git Bash.
*.sh text eol=lf

# NOT redundant with *.sh: .githooks/pre-commit has no extension, and it is the
# single most important script in the repo.
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# Batch files are the exception: older cmd.exe mis-parses a multi-line .cmd with
# LF endings, so these stay CRLF on purpose.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Generated / machine-compared files: pin them so a byte-for-byte check never
# reports "out of date" forever on identical content.
package-lock.json text eol=lf

# Binaries: never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.db binary
